  "interpretation": [
    "The modern walker validates node kinds and supports mappings, aliases, ranges, JSX, and custom protocols; the original walker supports a narrower native-node contract. Timings are absolute costs on one 91-node tree, not a general complexity claim.",
    "Source-only import peaks include compilation allocations. Current walker imports a small collection of stdlib helpers and avoids eager typing/dataclass dependencies; current utility imports generated Unicode tables.",
    "Utility legacy ES6 throughput uses identical inputs, but the old astral results are incorrect. Unicode17 classification and scalar/type validation are additional work."
  ]
